	(lib_symbols)
	(text "# BLOCK DIAGRAM & SUBSYSTEM INTERCONNECT DESIGN NOTES (REV 3.6)\n\nProject: OpenMycoNet COMBO_NODE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\n\n---\n\n### 1. HIERARCHICAL BUS ARCHITECTURE & INTERCONNECT MATRIX\n\n* Digital Core & Communication Buses:\n  * USB DATA Bus: Native USB 2.0 (`USB_D+`, `USB_D-`) routed from USB-C connector J1 (Sheet 4) through USBLC6-25C6 ESD protection array U1 and \n    27 Ω series resistors R3/R4 directly to ESP32-S3 USB transceiver (Sheet 7).\n  * Shared I2C Bus: Shared I2C BUS (`SDA`, `SCL`) pulled up via 4.7 kΩ resistors R17/R18 on MCU sheet, interfacing MAX17048 Fuel Gauge U5 (Sheet 6), \n    ADS1115 ADC U14 (Sheet 8), DS3231 RTC U10 (Sheet 8), and SCD41 CO2 Sensor U11 (Sheet 8).\n  * Shared SPI Bus: High-speed SPI (`SPI_CS`, `SPI_MOSI`, `SPI_SCK`, `SPI_MISO`) driving SX1262 LoRa Transceiver U16 (Sheet 9) and \n    Hirose DM3AT MicroSD Card Interface J13 (Sheet 10).\n  * Debug UART0 Bus: `TXD0` and `RXD0` lines from ESP32-S3 routed directly to Expansion Header J3 (Pins 8 & 10) for firmware flashing and \n    real-time terminal output.\n* Analog Signal & Excitation Control Nets:\n  * `DAC_OUT` / `DAC_STIM`: 16 Hz AC stimulation line generated by MCU DAC (GPIO17/Pin 38), filtered via RC low-pass network \n    (R38 = 1 kΩ, C29 = 10 nF relocated directly to U13 Pin 3 +INA), and routed through selectable OPA2320S buffer stage U13.\n  * `EC_ENABLE`: Dedicated digital line from ESP32-S3 (GPIO48/Pin 25) toggling TS5A3159 analog switch U15 for dual-mode biological impedance and \n     excitation path selection.\n  * `INA+` / `INA-`: Differential microvolt bio-potential sensing lines from J4 connector routed through R56/R57 1 kΩ series \n     current-limiting resistors into BAV199DW clamping array D3 and INA333 instrumentation amplifier U10.\n  * `MOISTURE_ANALOG`: Analog output from Soil Moisture Connector J9 routed to ADS1115 ADC U14 Channel AIN0 (Pin 4).\n\n---\n\n### 2. POWER OPTIMIZATION & DEEP SLEEP CONTROL NETS\n\n* `ANA_SHUT` (Analog Front-End Shutdown):\n  * Hierarchical Signal: Output from ESP32-S3 (GPIO42, Pin 35) routed directly to ~SHDN1 (Pin 5) and ~SHDN2 (Pin 10) of U13 (OPA2320SAIDGSR).\n  * Standby State: Pulled to GNDA via 10 kΩ resistor R23 on MCU sheet, forcing the analog front-end into ultra-low-power standby (< 1 µA) \n    during deep sleep.\n* MicroSD & Watchdog Power Gating:\n  * `SD_CARD_SLEEP` / `WCD_SLEEP`: Driven by ESP32-S3 GPIO47 (Pin 34) controlling U17 (TPS22919) high-side load switch and TPS3851 SET1 pin.\n  * Bus Leakage Protection: All SPI bus pull-ups (R48, R49, R51, R52) re-routed directly to the gated `SD_VDD` rail to eliminate parasitic \n    back-feeding when `SD_VDD` is switched off.\n* Soil Moisture Sensor Power Gating:\n  * `MOISTURE_SLEEP`: Driven by ESP32-S3 GPIO41 (Pin 34) controlling U18 (TPS22919) high-side load switch.\n  * Gated Rail Routing: Gates power rail `MOISTURE_VDD` directly to Pin 1 of J9 terminal, eliminating continuous 5 mA - 15 mA sensor idle \n    drain during sleep.\n  * ADC Power Isolation: ADS1115 ADC U14 VDD (Pin 8) remains tied to continuous clean analog power `+3.3VA` to keep the shared I2C bus active \n    without back-feeding through internal ESD diodes.\n* Static Power LED Elimination:\n  * Removed static PCB power indicator LEDs on +BATT and VDD supply rails, saving ~7.7 mA continuous quiescent power loss.\n\n---\n\n### 3. SYSTEM SAFETY, BATTERY & PROTECTION ARCHITECTURE\n\n* Charger & Power-Path Manager Configuration:\n  * Core IC: BQ24075 (U4) standalone Li-ion power-path manager on Sheet 6.\n  * Mode Setup: EN2 pin (Pin 5) pulled HIGH to VBUS via 10 kΩ resistor R12, and EN1 (Pin 6) grounded. Guarantees stable VDD system \n    power regulation during batteryless USB operation.\n  * Power Switch S1: Hardware slide switch connected to SYSOFF (Pin 15) to toggle system power ON/OFF.\n* External Battery Thermal Protection:\n  * TH1 NTC Status: On-board thermistor TH1 designated Do Not Populate (DNP) and removed from BOM/CPL to prevent parallel 10 kΩ resistance \n    interference (5 kΩ equivalent).\n  * NTC Routing: BQ24075 TS pin (Pin 1) relies 100% on the external battery pack NTC connected through J2 Pin 2.\n* Bio-Front-End Input Protection:\n  * `INA333` Clamping: INA+ and INA- differential inputs protected by 1 kΩ (0.1%) series current-limiting resistors R56 and R57 placed \n     in front of BAV199DW (D3) ultra-low-leakage rail-clamping diodes to absorb high-voltage ESD surges safely.\n* Watchdog Supervisor Timing:\n  * TPS3851H33 Window Watchdog U7: Driven by MCU `RST_WDI` (GPIO4/Pin 4).\n  * Reset Timeout: Hardware timer configured via 100 nF capacitor C45 for a nominal 323.4 ms watchdog timeout window (t_WD = 323.4 ms).\n  * Sleep Override: GPIO47 (`WCD_SLEEP`) pulls SET1 LOW prior to deep sleep to cleanly disable watchdog resets.\n\n---\n\n### 4. SUBSYSTEM INTERCONNECT & PERIPHERAL ISOLATION\n\n* Off-Board Blue Light LEDs:\n  * Interface: Connectors J5 and J6 configured as 2-pin Screw Terminals.\n  * Topology: Pin 1 connects to BATT+ power rail via 68 Ω series resistors (R33, R36)., Pin 2 connects to the Drain of low-side BSS138 N-channel MOSFETs Q1 and Q2.\n  * Drive Logic: Active-HIGH PWM drive via `LED_PWM1` (GPIO11/Pin 18) and `LED_PWM2` (GPIO10/Pin 17) with 10 kΩ gate pull-down resistors R59/R60.\n* EC Excitation Low-Pass Filter:\n  * RC Network: Filter capacitor C29 (10 nF) located directly at the non-inverting input (+INA / Pin 3) of U13 (OPA2320S) after series \n    resistor R38 (1 kΩ).\n  * Frequency Cutoff"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
